## Error Handling Review

When asked to review error handling:

- Flag silent catch blocks: catch/except/rescue with no log, no rethrow, no meaningful action.
- Flag inconsistent propagation: same error category handled with exceptions in some places and result types or error codes in others.
- Flag missing UI error states: components making network/DB calls with no error branch shown to the user.
- Flag raw error exposure: exception text, stack traces, or internal codes shown directly to the user.
- Flag retry without backoff: retry loops with no delay, no maximum cap, or retrying non-retryable errors.
- Flag unhandled boundaries: network calls, DB writes, or filesystem access with no explicit error handler.
- Flag untyped errors: errors propagated as raw strings or untyped objects instead of typed exception classes or result types.
- Flag undocumented error contracts: public APIs that can fail with no declared error types.
- Order findings P0 (silent catch on data-integrity path) through P3 (minor naming inconsistency) with file:line and a one-line fix.
